        "original_id": "995bad4f-dda4-5b5a-bd04-c51edd9f84a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Todd Phillips, Scot Armstrong, Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, DJ Qualls, Avery Kidd Waddell\n- Works: Road Trip, Old School, Starsky & Hutch, The Hangover Trilogy, Due Date, War Dogs, In Too Deep, The New Guy, Inside Schwartz, Law & Order, Without a Trace, Angel\n- Roles: writer, director, actor\n- Organizations: NBC\n\nFacts:\n- Todd Phillips is best known for writing and directing Road Trip (2000), Old School (2003), Starsky & Hutch (2004), The Hangover Trilogy (2009, 2011, and 2013), Due Date (2010), and War Dogs (2016).\n- Road Trip is a 2000 American comedy film directed by Todd Phillips and written by Scot Armstrong and Todd Phillips.\n- Road Trip stars Breckin Meyer, Seann William Scott, Paulo Costanzo, and DJ Qualls as four college friends who take an 1800-mile trip to recover an illicit tape mistakenly mailed to a girlfriend.\n- Inside Schwartz is an American sitcom that aired on NBC from September to December 2001 and starred Breckin Meyer in the title role.\n- Avery Kidd Waddell is an American director, writer, and actor who appeared in In Too Deep, Road Trip, and The New Guy and guest-starred on Law & Order, Without a Trace, and Angel.",
